Bring a large #pot of salted water to a boil. Add the @spaghetti, linguine or bucatini{16%ounces} and cook, stirring occasionally, until al dente. Reserve 1 1/2 cups pasta water, then drain the pasta.

Add the @unsalted butter{6%tablespoons}, @white miso{3%tablespoons} and 1 1/4 cups pasta water to the #pot and whisk over medium heat until miso breaks down and liquid is uniform, ~{1%minute} to ~{2%minutes}. Add the pasta and @Parmesan{4%ounces}(finely grated) and cook, stirring vigorously with #tongs until cheese is melted and sauce emulsifies.

> The key word here is "vigorously." To achieve a silky smooth pasta instead of a gloppy one, put your cacio e pepe skills to work.

Divide among shallow #bowls{} and sprinkle with @?kizami nori{}, furikake or thinly sliced seaweed snacks{}(for garnish), if using.